# Research integrity

This repository implements a Computational Linguistics project. Treat claims as hypotheses until experiments exist.

- Never fabricate metrics, citations, dataset statistics, or deployment status.
- Never show placeholder charts or invented model outputs as measured results.
- If a model, dataset, or calibration method is not configured, say so in the API and UI.
- SwordsmanImp is Chinese sitcom data. Do not silently translate it or call it an English corpus.
- Circa is primarily polar-question / indirect-answer pairs with situational context, not long multi-turn sitcom dialogue.
- Evidence spans must quote exact utterance text. Do not claim a speaker said something that was only implied.
- Generated natural-language explanations are not the model's internal reasoning.
- Fit TF-IDF and other learned preprocessors on training data only.
- Do not commit secrets, raw licensed dataset dumps, or checkpoints.
